Crux2 mode for PS2Recomp (ran-j/PS2Recomp eb8688b2fd191129f103a39543002c005b33409c). Copyright (C) 2026 Press5elect.
GPL-3.0-or-later, with the attribution term of Crux2's NOTICE: keep "Crux2 by Press5elect".
Also, in both modes: MOVZ and MOVN move the low 64 bits only, as the R5900 does (PS2Recomp moved all
128, so the upper half of the destination took the source's; found by Crux2's interpreter check).
In Crux2 mode (kit v1.3.3): every MMI instruction, the FPU's arithmetic and the SA instructions are
emitted as CRUX2_EE(<instruction word>), which Crux2's runtime runs with PCSX2's own interpreter code
(crux2_ee_interp.h): Crux2's instruction-by-instruction comparison found about 60 of PS2Recomp's
MMI and FPU translations giving other results than the processor (word orders, HI/LO, saturation,
multiply-add, SQRT.S's operand, the FPU's clamping), and PDIVBW dividing INT_MIN by -1 on the host.

